isUnmixed -- checks whether an ideal is unmixed
***********************************************

  * Usage: 
        isUnmixed I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

A function that checks whether an ideal $I \subseteq R$ is unmixed, that is,
whether the ideal $I$ satisfies $\dim(R/I) = \dim(R/P)$ for all associated
primes $P \in {\rm Ass}_R(R/I)$.

The following example uses  [SM, Example 1.6].

+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x_1..x_5];                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x_1*x_3, x_1*x_4, x_1*x_5, x_2*x_3, x_2*x_4, x_2*x_5);|
|                                                                     |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : isUnmixed I                                                     |
|                                                                     |
|o3 = false                                                           |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+

References
==========

[SM] Hero Saremi and Amir Mafi. Unmixedness and arithmetic properties of
matroidal ideals. Arch. Math. 114 (2020), no. 3 299–-304.

