    vertex decomposition is degenerate
  * *note CheckUnmixed: CheckUnmixed, -- check whether ideals encountered are
    unmixed
  * *note findOneStepGVD: findOneStepGVD, -- for which indeterminates does
    there exist a geometric vertex decomposition
  * *note getGVDIdeal: getGVDIdeal, -- computes the $C_{y,I}$ or $N_{y,I}$
    ideal at any point in the GVD recursion tree
  * *note isGVD: isGVD, -- checks whether an ideal is geometrically vertex
    decomposable
  * *note isLexCompatiblyGVD: isLexCompatiblyGVD, -- checks whether an ideal is
    <-compatibly geometrically vertex decomposable for a given order
  * *note isWeaklyGVD: isWeaklyGVD, -- checks whether an ideal is weakly
    geometrically vertex decomposable
  * *note oneStepGVDCyI: oneStepGVDCyI, -- computes the ideal $C_{y,I}$
  * *note oneStepGVDNyI: oneStepGVDNyI, -- computes the ideal $N_{y,I}$
  * *note UniversalGB: UniversalGB, -- whether the generators for an ideal form
    a universal Gröbner basis
  * *note Verbose: (Macaulay2Doc)Verbose, -- an optional argument

