SquarefreeOnly -- only return the squarefree variables from the generators
**************************************************************************

Description
===========

The algorithm for *note findOneStepGVD: findOneStepGVD, comprises two steps.
First, it checks the given generators for the given ideal $I$ and creates a
list of all indeterminates which appear squarefree in all of the generators.
For each of the remaining variables $y$, it then computes a Gröbner basis for
$I$ with respect to a $y$-compatible monomial order. If $y$ appears in the
elements of the Gröbner basis with only degree zero or degree one, then we have
a geometric vertex decomposition, and $y$ is appended to the list of
indeterminates.

If SquarefreeOnly=>true, then only the first half of the algorithm runs. This
option is used by the *note isGVD: isGVD, and *note isWeaklyGVD: isWeaklyGVD,
functions to avoid unnecessary duplicate computations of Gröbner bases.

See also
========

  * *note findOneStepGVD: findOneStepGVD, -- for which indeterminates does
    there exist a geometric vertex decomposition

